course: dictionary
lesson: 1376
title: Capacity: how much it can hold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word capacity has a few related meanings, and the clues around it tell you which one you need. Read the words next to it first. «The bottle has a capacity of one litre.» Here capacity means how much the bottle can hold.
explain: «The stadium has a capacity of 40,000.» This is not about skill. It means the largest number of people the place can hold. «The hall was full to capacity.» Full to capacity means so full that nothing more can fit.
explain: Capacity can also mean an ability to do something, or a role someone has. «She spoke in her capacity as head teacher.» Here capacity means her job, the position she holds. To check, swap in your meaning: "She spoke in her role as head teacher" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Capacity means the amount something can hold.
fact: Jugs and bottles have a capacity measured in litres (l) and millilitres (ml). There are 1000 millilitres in one litre.
fact: «Full to capacity» means completely full, with no room left.
fact: «The Yangtze is the longest river in Asia, about 6,300 km.» On it, the Three Gorges Dam has the largest capacity of any power station in the world, which means it can produce more power than any other.
exercise: «The jug has a capacity of two litres.» What does capacity mean here? | The number of people who use it | The colour of the jug | The price of the jug | *The amount the jug can hold
exercise: «The hall was full to capacity.» What does full to capacity mean? | Full of fun and noise | *So full that no more can fit | Empty and very quiet | Half full of water
exercise: Which sentence uses capacity to mean the most people a place can hold? | The jug has a capacity of 500 ml. | *The stadium has a capacity of 40,000. | Her capacity as a teacher is clear to see.
test: What unit would you use to measure «The bottle's capacity is 750», if it means the amount of drink it holds? | *Millilitres | Metres | Hours | Kilograms
test: What does capacity mean in «She spoke in her capacity as head teacher»? | *Her role or position | Her height | Her favourite hobby | The amount she can hold
exam: «The Three Gorges Dam is the largest power station in the world by capacity.» What does capacity mean in this sentence? | Its number of visitors | Its weight in tonnes | Its age in years | *Its ability to produce power
